{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["And sets it up in secret — all twelve curses correspond to the twelve tribes, and all of them are transgressions that are habitually done in secret, as I shall explain for each one — except for two that are sometimes done openly and sometimes in secret: idol worship and striking one's fellow. Therefore Scripture specifies 'in secret' for both of them, for regarding transgressions done openly they did not come to pronounce a curse, since the court will punish him for those done openly, as written at the end of all the curses: ״הנסתרות ליהוה אלהינו״ — He will take vengeance for the hidden ones, for they were cursed in the name of the Holy One, blessed be He; but ״הנגלות לנו ולבנינו עד עולם לעשות את כל דברי התורה הזאת״ — lashes, stoning, burning, slaying, and strangling. Do you not see that it is not written here: 'Cursed be he who lies with his fellow's wife'? For what business do you have entering another person's house — and they would not let him go unnoticed?!"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:39:34.540434381Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}